[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":6,\"end_line\":7,\"quoted_text\":\"once, assayed once for crude protein, and then stripped and retired. No vessel\\nwas reused, and no vessel was sampled or assayed more than once.\"},{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":10,\"end_line\":10,\"quoted_text\":\"Independent unit column: vessel_id\"}]},{\"description\":\"The 20 data rows carry 20 distinct vessel_id labels (V01 through V20); no label repeats, and each arm has exactly 10 rows (baseline: V01,V04,V05,V08,V09,V12,V13,V16,V17,V20; cu_amended: V02,V03,V06,V07,V10,V11,V14,V15,V18,V19).\",\"observed_value\":\"20 unique vessel_id values across 20 rows; 10 baseline, 10 cu_amended\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":3,\"quoted_text\":\"vessel_id,medium,seed_od600,final_titer_g_per_l\\nV01,baseline,0.41,4.8\\nV02,cu_amended,0.39,5.5\"},{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":20,\"end_line\":21,\"quoted_text\":\"V19,cu_amended,0.41,5.7\\nV20,baseline,0.42,5.0\"}]},{\"description\":\"The workflow explicitly counts occurrences of each vessel_id and would report any unit appearing more than once; each row's single titer is appended to its arm exactly once before the Welch t-test.\",\"observed_value\":\"Counter-based duplicate check; one append per row into arm lists\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":61,\"end_line\":63,\"quoted_text\":\"seen = Counter(row[UNIT_COLUMN] for row in rows)\\n    repeated = sorted(unit for unit, hits in seen.items() if hits > 1)\\n    repeated_note = \\\", \\\".join(repeated) if repeated else \\\"none\\\"\"},{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":65,\"end_line\":67,\"quoted_text\":\"titers = defaultdict(list)\\n    for row in rows:\\n        titers[row[ARM_COLUMN]].append(float(row[VALUE_COLUMN]))\"}]},{\"description\":\"The report's diagnostics confirm 20 rows, 20 independent vessels, and zero vessels appearing more than once, with 10 vessels per arm, consistent with the raw CSV.\",\"observed_value\":\"Rows read: 20; Independent vessels: 20; repeated vessels: none; n=10 per arm\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":6,\"end_line\":8,\"quoted_text\":\"- Rows read: 20\\n- Independent vessels: 20\\n- Vessels appearing more than once: none\"},{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":12,\"end_line\":13,\"quoted_text\":\"| baseline | 10 | 5.000 | 0.258 |\\n| cu_amended | 10 | 5.700 | 0.298 |\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The only mechanism that could admit a repeated unit is the arm-pooling loop, which appends rows keyed by medium without deduplicating by vessel_id; the Counter check is diagnostic only and does not filter. However, since the supplied CSV contains no repeated vessel_id, no repeated entry actually occurs.\",\"observed_value\":\"no filtering by unit, but no duplicates exist in the input data\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":66,\"end_line\":67,\"quoted_text\":\"for row in rows:\\n        titers[row[ARM_COLUMN]].append(float(row[VALUE_COLUMN]))\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I attempted to demonstrate the issue by searching for any vessel_id entering the row-independent Welch t-test more than once: I enumerated all 20 vessel_id values in data/input.csv (V01 through V20) and found each exactly once, with exactly 10 rows per medium arm; I traced the workflow to confirm every row contributes exactly one titer to exactly one arm list and that no join, resampling, or replicate expansion duplicates rows; and I cross-checked the reported arm means (5.000 and 5.700 g/L) and mean difference (0.700 g/L) against hand-computed values from the raw CSV, which matched, ruling out hidden duplication upstream of the reported statistics. No path by which an independent unit enters the procedure repeatedly could be constructed from the supplied files.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-j1-reviewer-fable-44","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:8f9167434bddfb4ffdc4","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The data description designates vessel_id as the independent-unit column and states each vessel was run and assayed exactly once and never reused.","observed_value":"vessel_id is the independent unit; no vessel reused or assayed more than once","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":6,"end_line":7,"quoted_text":"once, assayed once for crude protein, and then stripped and retired. No vessel\nwas reused, and no vessel was sampled or assayed more than once."},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":10,"end_line":10,"quoted_text":"Independent unit column: vessel_id"}]},{"description":"The 20 data rows carry 20 distinct vessel_id labels (V01 through V20); no label repeats, and each arm has exactly 10 rows (baseline: V01,V04,V05,V08,V09,V12,V13,V16,V17,V20; cu_amended: V02,V03,V06,V07,V10,V11,V14,V15,V18,V19).","observed_value":"20 unique vessel_id values across 20 rows; 10 baseline, 10 cu_amended","source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":1,"end_line":3,"quoted_text":"vessel_id,medium,seed_od600,final_titer_g_per_l\nV01,baseline,0.41,4.8\nV02,cu_amended,0.39,5.5"},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":20,"end_line":21,"quoted_text":"V19,cu_amended,0.41,5.7\nV20,baseline,0.42,5.0"}]},{"description":"The workflow explicitly counts occurrences of each vessel_id and would report any unit appearing more than once; each row's single titer is appended to its arm exactly once before the Welch t-test.","observed_value":"Counter-based duplicate check; one append per row into arm lists","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":61,"end_line":63,"quoted_text":"seen = Counter(row[UNIT_COLUMN] for row 